ve interpretation of age-specific mortality reductions from the Swedish breast cancer-screening trials</article-title><source>J Natl Cancer Inst</source><year>1995</year><volume>87</volume><fpage>1217</fpage><lpage>1223</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Natl Cancer Inst||87|1217||bib9|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7563167</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eeles</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Screening for hereditary cancer and genetic testing, epitomised by breast cancer</article-title><source>Eur J Cancer</source><year>1999</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>1954</fpage><lpage>1962</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Eur J Cancer||35|1954||bib10|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10711238</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ellman</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Is psychological well being impaired in long term survivors of breast cancer</article-title><source>J Med Screening</source><year>1995</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>5</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Med Screening||2|5||bib11|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Elmore</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Wells</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Howard</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Does diagnostic accuracy in mammography depend on radiologists' experience</article-title><source>J Women Health</source><year>1998</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>443</fpage><lpage>449</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Women Health||7|443||bib12|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation cit